#: quevedo.php:70
msgid "Disable post tags"
msgstr ""

#: quevedo.php:71
msgid "If not used properly, post tags can create a lot of duplicate content in your site. This feature hides them and redirects tag archives to your homepage."
msgstr ""

#: quevedo.php:74
msgid "Disable post formats"
msgstr ""

#: quevedo.php:75
msgid "If you are not using post formats, they only add clutter to the post editor."
msgstr ""

#: quevedo.php:78
msgid "Disable author archives"
msgstr ""

#: quevedo.php:79
msgid "If you have a single-user blog, the author archive will be exactly the same as your homepage. This could lead to duplicate content SEO issues."
msgstr ""

#: quevedo.php:82
msgid "Disable date archives"
msgstr ""

#: quevedo.php:83
msgid "Date archive pages (year, month and day) can create duplicate or thin content on personal blogs. This feature redirects them to your homepage."
msgstr ""

#: quevedo.php:86
msgid "Disable attachment pages"
msgstr ""

#: quevedo.php:87
msgid "WordPress can create a page for each uploaded file, which adds a lot of thin content. This feature redirects those pages to the file itself, as WordPress does by default on sites created with version 6.4 or later."
msgstr ""

#: quevedo.php:90
msgid "Simplify editor blocks"
msgstr ""

#: quevedo.php:91
msgid "When editing a blog post, the available blocks are reduced to: paragraph, heading, list, image, quote, separator, code, preformatted."
msgstr ""

#: quevedo.php:97
msgid "Add featured image to post metadata"
msgstr ""

#: quevedo.php:98
msgid "Outputs Open Graph and Twitter image meta tags with the post featured image, or with the default featured image if the post has none."
